{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>By the names of the tribes of their fathers, etc.</b> According to the words of Rabbi Yehoshiah, the verse comes to remove the plain sense heard from the saying ״לְאֵלֶּה״ — that the intent is not upon those counted in the plains of Moab, but rather the meaning is ״כְּאֵלֶּה״ — those who are twenty years old. And Rabbi Yonatan explains that the verse comes to say that although they apportioned to those counted in the plains of Moab, they in turn disinherited those who came out of Egypt and then inherited [the land] from them, as they said in the baraita (Sifrei), and this is their language: ״A similar case you find regarding those who entered the Land: this one took a se'ah and those took three se'ahs, and they disinherited their fathers, and the dead inherited through the living, and they apportioned anew equally.״ And according to this approach it is precisely examined correctly that He said <b>יִנְחָלוּ</b>, for He used the term for those who receive an inheritance — whereas until now the grammatical form was otherwise, as in His saying <b>תֵּחָלֵק הָאָרֶץ</b> and He did not say ״יַחְלְקוּ״; and so His saying <b>תַּרְבֶּה נַחֲלָתוֹ</b> etc.; and so His saying <b>יֻתַּן נַחֲלָתוֹ</b> and He did not say ״יִקַּח נַחֲלָתוֹ״; <b>יֵחָלֵק אֶת הָאָרֶץ</b> and He did not say ״יַחְלְקוּ הָאָרֶץ״. From this you have learned that until now the verse was speaking of what would be done in giving them possession, whereas the statement ״לִשְׁמוֹת etc. יִנְחָלוּ״ is what the inheritors would do after the inheritance reached them — they would inherit it in this manner, as though their fathers had inherited it from them and they return and inherit it from them. And this is His saying <b>יִנְחָלוּ</b>, for He did not mention the giver of the inheritance in order to clothe the matter in [that form]."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The baraita's phrase והורישו את אביהם וירשו המתים את החיים describes the dead (who left Egypt and died in the wilderness) inheriting through their living descendants; rendered hyper-literally to preserve the compressed rabbinic construction."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:00.412433132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}